From 56912ada481bfef19c20240781a7071da05edb78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:15:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Sharpened foliage coverage and quarter-resolution AO
 (F-223A)

- Foliage AA 1 = Sharp Coverage: coverage pixel shaders get their alpha
  sharpened to the alpha-test edge (SPIR-V patch, module key #sharp);
  hdAlphaAASharp (default 1)
- hdAOHalfRes 0 full / 1 half / 2 quarter: the AO work grid scale is
  1/2/4 in flags.w; centre, upsample tent and reprojection follow it
- All nine AO headers regenerated with shader-work/ao_spv.py

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
